# Use the highest models (applies to EVERY agent and subagent)

The user explicitly wants this, and does not care about token cost: "I don't care about spending more tokens, I got money."

## Default
- **Go very heavy on higher/highest models** for reasoning, planning, decision making, thinking, research, debugging, reviews, data pipelines, and model/training design.
- When in doubt → pick the **highest** model. Never downgrade to save cost or time.
- Fast/cheap models only for trivial lookups (e.g., find a file).

## Subagents
- Hard or thinking-heavy sub-work → subagent on the **strongest available model** (latest top-tier Claude Opus thinking-high, or latest top GPT).
- **Copy this rule into every subagent prompt** so subagents also follow it.
- Tell the user which model was used and for what.

## Remind the user (mandatory)
- The user runs Cursor on **Auto**; agents cannot change the main chat model.
- **Before any hard task** (planning, big decisions, new pipelines, training design, debugging tricky results, reviews): remind the user to **switch from Auto to the highest model** — at the top of the reply, one short line, every time.
- Also remind when a conversation turns hard mid-way.
